Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:29:20 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows 10 Mobile: Chrome for Android's toolbar and menu

The toolbar as on Chrome for Android: home, the address bar, a new tab
button and the tab count in a rounded square, the menu. The count opens
the list of tabs (tab search, anchored to it), so tab search's own
toolbar icon goes again. Home is on by default.

The menu as Chrome for Android's, instead of the desktop's: a first row
of round icons -- back, forward, bookmark, download (save the page) and
reload -- then a new tab; history and clearing browsing data; downloads,
bookmarks and recent tabs; settings and help; and the shell's own
submenu. No incognito (one process, one profile's storage).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
